A||N||3||tpkrat1||86 SE Run Problem(s)||||1||
Z||000000||tpkrat1||05-06-2001||12:34 PM||||Recently accquired an 86 SE auto 2.8 V-6 from the original non smoker lady owner.(musta been blond cause she bought a Camry 3 years ago and parked this under a tree in her back yard)I dumped fresh gas and jump started it and drove it home (26 miles). Did the usual cleaning and detailing in and out and then started on the driveline. Changed out the plugs (even the rusted ones on the back side)cap rotor and wires,A/C belt and alt belt,air and fuel filters. bought a new battery too. started it up and it runs like sh** nothing like it was when i drove it home. pulled code from diagnostic panel in center consol and other than the 12 is showed a 44 for the O2 Sensor.the only other thing i have done in reguard to the mech side is take some 1500 grit sandpaper and clean the stator in the distributor as it and the shaft for the rotor were very rusty.still runs real rough with no power and it stalls out when you put it in any gear inc reverse. any ideas out there?  Thnx for any help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||05-06-2001||01:31 PM||||Are you sure the plug wires are on the correct plugs?  I had a similar problem several years ago after a major tuneup and discovered I'd gotten some of the plug wires crossed up.  It ran like crap until I straightened it out <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I seem to remember it setting an O2 sensor code too.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||05-06-2001||03:29 PM||||Rodrv6 has a point...def check to make sure the wires are going to the appropriate plugs. You also may want to check the timing...you may have inadvertantly bumped the distributor..<BR>Oh yeah, also make sure you gapped the new plugs correctly. M7F<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 05-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||tpkrat1||05-08-2001||06:20 PM||||Is the firing order for all General Motors 2.8 V-6 the same? (i.e. rt front is #1? with right side being the side closest to the trunk wall and not up against passenger compartment?) That is where I started the firing order according to where the cap wires led.I was thinking that possibly from cleaning the stator in the dist I might have threw it an eyelash off timing wise. Been real busy at work so am not able to get back online but every other day. Thanxs for help  mike||||reg||1
